    {
      "argv": [
        "node",
        "/Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/tools/swarm-917312983/dist/cli.js",
        "Mime.getType(path) (src/Mime.ts) derives a type from the extension after the last dot of the last path segment. The two regular expressions that strip the directory part and the part before the extension do not match across line terminators, so a file name that contains one is typed wrongly: getType('LINE\\nFEED.png') returns null instead of 'image/png', and the same happens for a carriage return (U+000D), a line separator (U+2028) and a paragraph separator (U+2029), with or without a directory part in front. This matters where the file name comes from an untrusted source: a content type decided from it must come from the extension after the last dot of the last segment, whatever characters precede it, so that a name crafted with a line terminator cannot make the lookup fail or pick an earlier extension. Make getType treat every line terminator like any other character when it strips the directory part and the extension's prefix; a space or tab in the name already works and must keep working. getExtension, define and the rest of the class stay as they are. The change belongs in src/Mime.ts only. Repository rules: keep the file's existing style, no new dependencies, no edits under test or types, and the whole suite (npm test, which builds first) must keep passing.\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npm run build && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.",
